The release-gate fix, **#7073**, is now in the merge queue. The reviewer (61f0abcc) approved head `9c3bb21b69` without changes. Their check matches mine:

- the sorting helper sorts the nested evidence when it is JSON and returns plain text unchanged;
- default builds produce identical text;
- nothing is stored;
- the expected file is untouched.

I marked the PR ready at the same head and told the CI monitor. Following the queue rules, I'm not watching CI. The monitor will tell me if the queue rejects the PR or if the next release gate still fails on this Kotlin case. I'm keeping the worktree `.mj/lanes/6112-kotlin` and the `/tmp/6112-kotlin` logs until it lands.

You still need to decide on:
- **#6685 M3/M4:** I recommend holding both while the native-engine lanes own the Go and JVM store files.
- **#6409 M6:** what scope you want.
- **#6862 and #6704:** whether to pick them up.
